-THE OPTIONAL `data` OPERAND (s172). An ECharts-primary IR is metadata-only by design (data:{values:[]}, encoding:{}) — the chart's nodes, links, rows and geometry live in viz.render's data branch and never enter the IR. Pass that SAME branch as `data` (exactly one of hierarchy | sankey | chord | network | geo, matching the mark trait) and certify lights two more pillars for these types AND runs the a11y-equivalence rules warn-first over it. Omit it and those two pillars stay 'unchecked' with a note naming the missing operand, and no a11y rule runs. `data` on a CARTESIAN spec is a structured error (OODS-V123): those certify from the IR alone, so it would be dead input.
