-DETERMINISM. Cartesian: two independent Vega-Lite compiles, byte-compared, hashed — PLUS two independent @oods/viz-render renders byte-compared for every cartesian chart, including contrast-exempt charts (the first reported as the OPTIONAL determinism.renderHash; a nondeterministic render fails `stable` and pulls conformant false — the pillar is falsifiable, not a compile tautology). ECharts-primary WITH `data`: contentHash identifies the retained projected option from the first of two independent adapter emissions and still equals viz.render's for the same (spec, data) pair. renderHash identifies the first normalized SVG whenever server-side rendering succeeds; the second independently emitted option is rendered as the proof, and `stable` requires both option and render equality. A typed first-render fault keeps contentHash, omits renderHash, and makes stable false; bubble_map without inline geometry keeps the option proof and names the no-server-map limitation. The certified runtime contract and render-hash epoch live at packages/viz-render/certified-matrix.json. Scope, stated: certify claims nothing about what the CALLER rendered (the render leg is certify's own deterministic render); the render never feeds contentHash; and cross-process renderHash identity is bounded by the locally certified runtime axes in that record.
+ACCESSIBILITY. The 16 equivalence rules evaluate the operand-built table and narrative. Error-severity failures fail the ECharts pillar and conformance. Warnings stay visible without failing the pillar. Findings keep their native severity. a11yNotApplicable lists rules whose declared preconditions were absent; absence is not a meaningful pass. This channel is present when the ECharts engine completed, including [] if no rule was inapplicable, and absent for spec-only, Cartesian or incomplete engine evaluations. A completed engine with an individual rule fault retains its findings and not-applicable results while failing the pillar. An evaluator fault cannot produce a passing accessibility pillar.
 
-ACCURACY. Cartesian: four declared reader-only structural rules over the IR + the compiled spec — non-zero bar baseline (OODS-V150), dual axis (V151), area-encodes-linear (V152), aggregation-hiding (V153). ECharts-primary WITH `data`: a per-type set over the operand — treemap/sunburst V154 (a node value area or angle cannot encode) and V155 (an explicit parent that is not the sum of its children); sankey V156 (negative or non-finite link value), V157 (a node height that is not the flow its links carry) and V158 (a duplicate directed flow); chord V156; choropleth V159 (a region matched to rows with CONFLICTING joined values). force_graph, bubble_map and flow_map offer NOTHING — a stated position, not a gap, and s173 m01 splits it because the two halves differ: force_graph's distortion candidates are adapter constants, while bubble_map's colorScale and flow_map's strengthField ARE authorable through the branch and simply have no rule written for them yet (a scope decision on the record, not an impossibility). No scorer, no corpus, no render step; the rules read, so the contentHash is unmoved by them.
+ACCURACY. Cartesian rules read the IR and compiled spec: non-zero bar baseline (V150), dual axis (V151), area scaling (V152), undisclosed aggregation (V153). ECharts rules read data: invalid hierarchy values/non-additive parents (V154/V155); invalid sankey/chord link values (V156); inconsistent sankey node throughput/duplicate links (V157/V158); conflicting choropleth join values (V159); negative or non-finite bubble size (OODS-V168), radius-based bubble scaling (OODS-V169), conflicting rows at the same bubble coordinates (OODS-V170), negative or non-finite flow strength (OODS-V171), duplicate directed geographic flows (OODS-V172), and duplicate directed force-graph links (OODS-V173). Reciprocal graph links and reciprocal geographic flows are distinct. Bubble scaling reads the public renderer's default linear size behavior; certification does not repair its pixels. accuracyRules lists offered codes, while accuracySummary counts only rules whose preconditions resolved. Pass means no offered rule detected its distortion, not a general promise of accuracy; zero evaluated ECharts rules is unchecked and cannot yield conformant:true.
 
-READ accuracy:'pass' PRECISELY: none of the rules OFFERED for that chart type positively detected its distortion — not that the chart is accurate. accuracySummary.rulesEvaluated says how many actually resolved their operand. On the ECharts path 'pass' additionally requires rulesEvaluated > 0, so zero resolved rules reports 'unchecked' with a note saying whether the offered set was empty or a precondition was absent. findings[] therefore carries THREE families told apart by code: OODS-A11Y-<rule.id>, OODS-V150..V153, OODS-V154..V159. On the CARTESIAN path a firing rule pulls conformant false; on the uncertified path conformant STAYS null (no folded claim is made there), so read pillars.accuracy and findings[].
+DETERMINISM. Two independent compiler/adapter emissions are compared and rendered independently. contentHash identifies the first canonical compiled spec or projected ECharts option; renderHash identifies its normalized SVG and matches viz.render for the same operand/scope. Stable requires both identities to repeat. A first-render fault keeps contentHash, omits renderHash and fails stability. A bubble_map without inline geometry keeps the option proof, omits renderHash and names the no-server-map limitation. Proof is bounded by packages/viz-render/certified-matrix.json and covers certify's own rendering, not a caller's rendering.
 
-A11Y-EQUIVALENCE runs WARN-FIRST for these 8. Supply `data` and the 16-rule equivalence engine evaluates over the operand-built table and narrative, each rule reporting pass, fail, or NOT-APPLICABLE with its absent precondition named — so an absent precondition is no longer indistinguishable from a meaningful pass. Failures reach findings[] as OODS-A11Y-<rule.id> at their NATIVE severity (an error-severity rule reports 'error'; nothing is remapped and nothing blocks). Not-applicable rules reach the top-level a11yNotApplicable[] channel as {rule, preconditionAbsent} in rule order — present (as [] when no rule was not-applicable) exactly when the engine ran on this data-backed path, and ABSENT on a {spec}-only call, on the cartesian path, and when the engine faulted (the partial list is discarded and notes[] says so). A not-applicable rule never enters findings[]. pillars.a11yEquivalence stays 'unchecked' on this path DELIBERATELY: warn-first enumerates what enforcement will require without moving a verdict, and the flip to pass/fail is a future enforce step. Without the operand there is nothing to evaluate and no a11y findings appear. The accessible table and narrative are generated on the data-backed path.
+CONTRAST. Cartesian charts and ECharts calls with data grade actual rendered paints. Role C checks mark-to-canvas WCAG 3:1; Role A checks categorical CIEDE2000 distinguishability across normal vision and three CVD simulations, retaining recycled-palette duplicates. Missing baked OODS palette bytes cannot produce contrast:'pass'. The three geo families retain the standing contrast exemption with their render evidence; this includes ordinal bubble maps. Spec-only ECharts calls retain the reconstructed palette grade and caveat. Cartesian conformance still fails for fail or ungradeable contrast/accuracy; unchecked and exempt retain their existing semantics. Read every pillar's enum, including ungradeable. contrastResults reports the requested theme/brand and measurement evidence; exemptions do not claim a canvas ratio.
 
-CONTRAST is RENDER-MEASURED for the 5 cartesian types: certify renders the compiled spec through @oods/viz-render and grades the SERIES-TO-PAINT ASSIGNMENT the data marks actually carry — duplicates retained, so a recycled palette (more consumed series than baked hexes) truthfully fails as a ΔE00=0 pair — against the requested CSS scope canvas: role-C mark-vs-background WCAG 3:1 (normative) + role-A categorical CIEDE2000 distinguishability (min-over-CVD), config.tokens overrides honoured. Unit classification still reads the compiled bytes, so a chart that baked no OODS palette can never certify contrast:'pass', and non-palette paints are author chrome — skipped, never failed. ECharts contrast is render-measured when `data` is supplied: visible chart fills and strokes feed Role C, the semantic N-long category assignment feeds Role A with genuine recycling duplicates retained, and the two grades combine by worst verdict. The 5 categorical families are graded; the 3 geo families remain exempt while still retaining normalized render evidence. spec-only calls retain the reconstructed baked-palette verdict and its baked-bytes caveat. An ordinal-categorical bubble_map colour is still not graded — as of s172 that rests on the exempt-all-geo ruling alone, since `data` exposes the colorField and the colorScale it renders on (s173 m01 corrects s172's wording: the RANGE is reachable on no path — the branch has no range field, so an ordinal bubble_map paints from Forge's own categorical list). contrastResults retains the requested theme/brand, verdict and measurement evidence; exempt and unchecked results do not claim a canvas ratio.
-
-THEME AND BRAND (s190): theme light|dark and brand A|B select the same scoped CSS colors as viz.render; defaults are light/A. data-backed ECharts paints come from the rendered projected option; geo render evidence remains exempt with no canvas ratio. HC token exports exist, but HC pixels are deferred. accuracyRules names the offered rule codes; accuracySummary.rulesEvaluated still counts only resolved operands.
-
-IF YOUR CLIENT CACHES THIS TEXT (s173 m01): tool EXECUTION is read fresh from the built server on every call, so a Forge update reaches your results immediately — but this description and the input schema are what your connector advertised AT CONNECT TIME, so after a Forge release you are reading the old contract until you RECONNECT. When a Forge changelog says an input or a verdict moved, reconnect before trusting the schema you already have. |
+SCOPE. Theme light|dark and brand A|B select the same CSS scope as rendering, default light/A. HC token exports exist, but HC pixels remain deferred. After a release that changes a schema or verdict, reconnect clients that cache tool descriptions and schemas. |
 | [fidelity.preview](./fidelity-preview.md) | Render an Object Catalog manifest through one of the non-production HTML fidelity emitters (boxes-arrows, wireframe, review, branded-mockup). Supply EXACTLY ONE manifest source: a named server-resident `fixture` (allow-listed — no caller-supplied paths) or an inline `manifest` object (data only, never a path; must contain an `entities` array). Returns complete HTML ready to insert into a preview surface; `options` control the projection variant, brand overlay (branded-mockup only), review threshold, and the inline <style> block. Branded mockups resolve built A/B light-scope tokens; brand-a/brand-b are deprecated aliases supported for one release. Unknown brands return OODS-BM-002 instead of falling back. Portable callers must provide inline manifest data because named fixtures are not shipped. |
 | [map](./map.md) | Grouped mapping-registry tool. Set `action` to one of apply|create|list|resolve|update|delete to select the operation; the remaining fields match that action's contract. Consolidates the former map.* tools with identical per-action behavior. Records and resolves mappings for external consumers; no composer or generator consumes them. preferred_terms and disambiguation_decisions are preserved and surfaced, not consumed by resolution. |
 | [schema](./schema.md) | Grouped schema-store tool. Set `action` to one of save|load|list|delete. Consolidates the former schema.* tools with identical per-action behavior. Use action=save to persist a composed UiSchema beyond the 30-minute schemaRef TTL. Saved schemas expose monotonic versions and schemaRef identity, not ETags or conditional requests. |
