   <h2 id="charts"><span class="n">09</span>Charts and dashboards</h2>
   <p>The <a href="viz/taxonomy.md">versioned taxonomy</a> classifies 34 chart identities (13 types and 21 patterns) across eight families and records each Core Analytics Profile cell as surface-complete or a typed gap.</p>
   <p><span class="k">viz.render</span> takes data and returns a chart specification. Thirteen chart types: <b>bar, line, area, scatter, heatmap</b> (from tabular rows; compiled to Vega-Lite, ECharts on request) and <b>treemap, sunburst, sankey, chord, force graph, choropleth, bubble map, flow map</b> (from node/link/geometry inputs; ECharts). Four input modes: a catalog pattern identity, explicit (chart type + encodings), suggest (rows only — the recommender picks), or a structured intent (goal, measures, dimensions). Pattern mode uses bundled authored data and presentation; unsupported interaction or layout is a typed authoring-only result (OODS-V167), and conflicting explicit operands return OODS-V166. The five Cartesian families return spec; the eight ECharts-primary families omit spec and return echartsSpec with output.echarts forced true and reason echarts-primary-family. Every successful result carries a content hash of the canonical spec; on request it also returns an accessible data table and a generated narrative derived from the same data. The 16 chart traits (marks, encodings, scales, layouts, interactions) are the vocabulary the spec is normalised into.</p>
